recommend check-in (Keaton) -- TWO seats now, and the second is a wall rather than a question. construction/REDS.md holds six rows, every one OPEN, and their bytes alone pass the 24,576 bound: this lap's two rows fit only by being cut across five passes, and the next red has no room at all. reds_fold.sh refusing OPEN rows was booked as a tidy seat and is now the thing standing between the tree and its own ledger -- a shelf for open rows with a pointer in the pin, a raised bound for this one page as session-logs/README.md already has, or something else, is yours. The other seat this lap named and declined to take: whether the roster's own witness can be rostered at all, when its scan refuses on any red the run card holds and its own red would land there. Splitting the card reading from the roster reading is one answer and a self-exempt row is another; both change how the tree measures itself, which is yours. Mechanically the next Pond lap is orbit two -- the declarations driven into grants through Caravan's capability pieces -- and that brushes Dream's lane, so it wants his nod first. This pier's tools/e/enclosure.conf still pins two elders and is gitignored, which stays your hand.
